course: dictionary
lesson: 10235
title: Tofu: a plant protein
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tofu is a soft white food made from soya milk that has been pressed into blocks. It is eaten a lot in China, Japan and other Asian countries, and it is a popular food with vegetarians.
explain: Tofu is a source of protein instead of meat. Look at the context: «Beans, lentils, nuts, tofu and eggs give plenty of protein to people who do not eat meat.» Tofu is on the list of protein foods for people who do not eat meat.
explain: Tofu mostly takes on the taste of the sauce or soup it is cooked in. You can fry it, add it to soups, or stir-fry it. When you meet a new food word, ask: what does the sentence tell me about it?
fact: Tofu is also called bean curd.
fact: Tofu is made from soya beans, which is why it is called a plant protein.
fact: Tofu is uncountable, so you say «some tofu», not «a tofu» or «three tofus».
fact: «Calcium» is found in tofu, along with milk, cheese, yoghurt and green vegetables.
fact: Tofu is often met in school dinners and Asian restaurants.
exercise: What is tofu made from? | Cow's milk left out to dry | Pressed sugar cubes | Soft white bread | *Soya milk pressed into blocks
exercise: «Beans, lentils, nuts, tofu and eggs give plenty of protein to people who do not eat meat.» What does tofu give to people who do not eat meat? | Salt | Water | Sugar | *Protein
exercise: «The adult brain is soft like tofu.» What does this tell you about tofu? | Tofu is sweet like jam | *Tofu is soft to the touch | Tofu is crunchy like a biscuit | Tofu is hard like a rock
test: Tofu takes on the taste of the sauce. Why might a cook put tofu in a stir-fry? | Because it is made of meat | Because it is sweet like sugar | Because it must be eaten raw | *Because it soaks up the flavour of the sauce
test: Vegans and vegetarians eat tofu. Which word names a food that gives you protein instead of meat? | Biscuit | Crisps | *Tofu | Sugar
exam: Tofu is uncountable. Which sentence is correct? | I ate many tofu for lunch. | I ate a tofu for lunch. | I ate tofus for lunch. | *I ate some tofu for lunch.
